.TH tapectl-snapshot-mark-reclaimable 1  "tapectl-snapshot-mark-reclaimable " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-snapshot\-mark\-reclaimable \- Mark a snapshot as reclaimable (with enforced preconditions)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl snapshot mark\-reclaimable\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] <\fB\-\-version\fR> [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mark a snapshot as reclaimable (with enforced preconditions)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR \fI<VERSION>\fR
Snapshot version
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Confirm in advance, as the global \-\-yes does: mark the version even though the version superseding it is short of its policy\*(Aqs min_copies or required_locations (for a tape\-only unit, the multiplied floors). Without either flag a terminal asks, and a non\-interactive run refuses, naming the shortfall. Only \-\-force (not \-\-yes, not a prompt) marks a version no current version supersedes — that releases the unit\*(Aqs only current version
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home.
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Unit name
